            <ArticleTitle>[The CT diagnosis of hemorrhages into the abdominal musculature resulting from therapeutic procedures on the coagulation system].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>150-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eleven patients treated by anticoagulants or lytic therapy suffered bleeding into the abdominal muscles, resulting in neurological symptoms or those of an acute abdomen. By means of CT it was possible to demonstrate the bleeds and to clarify the differential diagnosis, thereby leading to correct treatment. The possibility of early diagnosis of haemorrhages makes CT a suitable and reliable method.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
